  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An Eastern Pacific trough of low\npressure will approach the coast of Northern California this\nafternoon. This will tighten the surface pressure gradient,\nresulting in sustained south to southwest winds 15 to 20 mph, with\ngusts near 30 mph this afternoon into this evening. A few strong\nthunderstorms are anticipated in Eastern Elko County this\nafternoon into this evening. The primary thunderstorm hazards will\nbe wind gusts near 45 mph and dangerous cloud to ground lightning\nstrikes. A cooling trend is expected today and Wednesday. By \nWednesday afternoon, high temperatures throughout Northern and \nCentral Nevada will be around ten degrees below normal for this \ntime of year. \n\nAn upper level area of low pressure will make landfall along the\ncoast of the Pacific Northwest Thursday. This cyclone aloft will\nmeander around the coast of the Pacific Northwest Friday into the\nupcoming weekend. Meanwhile, a tropical cyclone will be located in\nthe Eastern Pacific, just west of the Baja Peninsula this weekend.\nThere are indications that these two storm systems may interact\nwith each other, drawing atmospheric moisture northward. Forecast\nconfidence is slowly increasing regarding this scenario.\nRegardless, timing, coverage, and extent of any precipitation \nlate this weekend into early next week will need to be further \nrefined in the upcoming few days. Here are probabilities of one\ntenth of an inch of rain or more fore select locations in Northern\nand Central Nevada from 5 AM PDT Sunday, September 6th, 2026 until\n5 AM PDT Tuesday, September 8th, 2026:\n\nEly - 65%\nWells - 55%\nJackpot - 55%\nWest Wendover - 50%\nElko - 45%\nSpring Creek - 45%\nTonopah - 45%\nEureka - 45%\nCarlin - 45%\nOwyhee - 40%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Forecast confidence is moderate\nregarding a few strong thunderstorms in Eastern Elko County this\nafternoon into this evening. Forecast confidence is high in breezy\nconditions throughout Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon\ninto this evening. Forecast confidence is high regarding a cooling\ntrend today and Wednesday. Forecast confidence is slowly\nincreasing regarding periods of rain late this weekend into early\nnext week. No deviations from the NBM model output.",
